thig5.8:3.1 starts: Having purified the divine eye
thig5.8:3.2 starts: while still a trainee,
thig5.8:3.3 starts: I know my previous lives,
thig5.8:3.4 starts: where I lived in the past.
thig5.12:2.1 starts: So, taking a staff & bowl in hand,
thig5.12:2.2 starts: begging for alms from house to house,
thig5.12:2.3 starts: feverish from the cold & heat,
thig5.12:2.4 starts: I wandered for seven full years.
thig6.2:2.1 starts: living along the side of the road,
thig6.2:2.2 starts: in cemeteries & heaps of trash,
thig6.2:2.3 starts: for three full years,
thig6.2:2.4 starts: afflicted with hunger & thirst.
thig5.6:3.1 starts: Then, sitting in my dwelling,
thig5.6:3.2 starts: I suddenly came to my senses:
thig5.6:3.3 starts: I’m following a miserable path.
thig5.6:3.4 starts: I’m under the sway of
thig5.10:2.1 starts: So why is it that I,
thig5.10:2.2 starts: a doer of the teacher’s bidding,
thig5.10:2.3 starts: don’t gain unbinding?
thig5.10:2.4 starts: I’m not lazy or proud.”
thig5.10:3.1 starts: Washing my feet,
thig5.10:3.2 starts: I noticed
thig5.10:3.3 starts: And in watching it flow from high
thig5.10:3.4 starts: to
thig5.10:5.1 starts: And taking a pin,
thig5.10:5.2 starts: I pulled out the wick:
thig5.10:5.3 starts: Like the flame’s unbinding
thig5.10:5.4 starts: was the liberation
thig5.11:2.1 starts: Do the Awakened One’s bidding,
thig5.11:2.2 starts: which, having done,
thig5.11:2.3 starts: Intent on tranquility of awareness,
thig5.11:2.4 starts: do the Awakened One’s bidding.
thig5.11:2.5 starts: Quickly:
thig5.11:2.6 starts: go sit to one side.”
thig5.11:5.1 starts: Getting up, they bowed down to her feet.
thig5.11:5.2 starts: “We have done your bidding.
thig5.11:5.3 starts: Like the thirty devas honoring Indra,
thig5.11:5.4 starts: unvanquished in battle,
thig5.11:5.5 starts: we—
thig5.11:5.6 starts: will continue honoring you.”
thig6.1:6.1 starts: Today—with arrow removed,
thig6.1:6.2 starts: without hunger, entirely
thig6.1:6.3 starts: to the Buddha, Dhamma, & Saṅgha I go,
thig6.1:6.4 starts: for refuge to
thig6.2:1.1 starts: Overwhelmed with grief for my son—
thig6.2:1.2 starts: naked, demented,
thig6.2:1.3 starts: my hair disheveled
thig6.2:1.4 starts: I went about here & there,
thig6.3:2.1 starts: Khemā:
thig6.3:2.2 starts: of this putrid body—
thig6.3:2.3 starts: disintegrating, dissolving.
thig6.3:2.4 starts: Sensual craving
thig6.5:3.1 starts: I will give in return
thig6.5:3.2 none
thig6.5:3.3 starts: eight times her weight
thig6.5:3.4 starts: in jewels & gold.”
